NOTICE

Built with Llama.

The real-model experiments recorded under sideband/ loaded Meta Llama
checkpoints from the Hugging Face Hub: meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct as
the verifier of the speculative-decoding pair and as the S1 harvest model,
and meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct as the draft (sideband/docs/THIRD_PARTY.md
names where each is pinned in the code). No checkpoint weights of those models
are shipped. The sideband folder carries model-output files produced with them,
among them token-id arrays and vocabulary strings under sideband/results/
(sideband/docs/THIRD_PARTY.md and sideband/docs/RELEASE_NOTES.md section 5
discuss them), and two small files of trained probe weights derived from the
harvested activations, sideband/results/real/k3_probe_weights.npz and
sideband/results/real/oq15_head_weights.npz; whether such a probe is "an AI
model" under the licences' naming clause for models trained on Llama outputs
is the owner's reading, not stated here. The amber folder's model use, stated by its survey of 2026-10-17:
meta-llama/Llama-3.2-3B as the target and meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B as the draft of
the P1 corpus and of the P4 to P6 archives (both base checkpoints), and
meta-llama/Llama-3.2-1B-Instruct and TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0
(Apache-2.0 by its model card, read 2026-10-17) for the rank-stability census
experiments (amber's F-5 to F-7 and F-10 name the checkpoint of each arm); the
folder carries model-output files produced with them: the P1 generate shards
(the target's generated token ids), the P1 rank and log-probability shards
and the P4 to P6 archive and symbol files under amber/results/, and no
checkpoint weights. The lockstep folder runs no neural model (its two
reference models are byte models) and carries no model-output
file and no checkpoint weights (its survey of 2026-10-18); its
F-12 to F-18 restate or recompute amber's measurements of the checkpoints
named above. The Llama 3.1 and 3.2 community
licences list "outputs or results" separately from the Llama Materials they
govern; this notice and the licence copies are included anyway. That is a
reading of the licence text, not legal advice.

